{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Of David. Fret not</b> — Some say: תתחר is from the hithpa'el binyan, from the root of חרון." "And the meaning of במרעים — on account of those who do evil. And it is on the pattern of: do not provoke yourself against them. And some say: like תתחרה את הסוסים, even though it is from the kal binyan."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:50.325975821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}